---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ui } from '../../i18n/ui';

const t = ui.en.privacy;
---

<Base title={t.title} description={t.title}>
	<article class="prose">
		<h1>Cavinum — Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="prose__updated">Last updated: September 5, 2026</p>

		<h2>What Cavinum is</h2>
		<p>
			Cavinum is a personal home wine-cellar inventory app.
		</p>

		<h2>What data the app processes</h2>
		<p>
			Your collection data (wine names, varieties, cabinets/shelves, notes, and photos you add
			yourself) is stored locally, in your browser — in a SQLite database built on OPFS (Origin
			Private File System). This data never leaves your device unless you explicitly enable Google
			Drive sync.
		</p>
		<p>
			The app has no server or database of its own. The developer has no access to your collection
			data under any circumstances.
		</p>

		<h2>Google Drive sync (optional)</h2>
		<p>
			If you connect your Google account, the app requests the Google OAuth drive.file scope — a
			restricted Google permission that grants access only to files the app itself has created. The
			app creates a single file (cavinum.db) inside a dedicated "Cavinum" folder in your Drive, and
			cannot see, read, or modify any other files, folders, or data in your Google account.
		</p>
		<p>
			The authorization-code-to-token exchange technically passes through the developer's own proxy
			server (a Cloudflare Worker), required by the OAuth protocol. The proxy does not store or log
			your tokens or any personal data — it only relays the request to Google and returns the
			response.
		</p>
		<p>
			Google Drive access tokens are stored locally in your browser (localStorage) and are never
			sent to the developer or any third party.
		</p>
		<p>
			When you first connect Google Drive, the app sends the developer a single message with your
			email address, your chosen access tier (free/Pro), and the connection time. This is used only
			for internal usage statistics and is never published or shared with third parties.
		</p>

		<h2>What the app does NOT do</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>No selling or sharing your data with third parties.</li>
			<li>No data collection without your explicit action (adding a wine, connecting Drive, etc.).</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Managing your data</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				You can disconnect Google Drive at any time in the app's settings — local tokens are
				removed from your device immediately.
			</li>
			<li>
				The cavinum.db file in your Google Drive remains entirely under your control — you can
				delete it directly via drive.google.com at any time.
			</li>
			<li>
				You can clear all local app data via your browser's site data settings, or via the app's
				own export/reset feature if available.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Children</h2>
		<p>The app is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect data specifically targeting children.</p>

		<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
		<p>If how the app processes data changes materially, this page will be updated with a new date above.</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			For questions about this policy — via{' '}
			<button type="button" class="prose__inline-link" data-open-feedback
				>feedback form</button
			>
		</p>
	</article>

	<style>
		.prose {
			width: 100%;
			max-width: 40rem;
			margin-inline: auto;
			padding-inline: clamp(1rem, 5vw, 3rem);
		}

		.prose h1 {
			font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
			line-height: 1.2;
			margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
		}

		.prose__updated {
			color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 65%, transparent);
			font-size: 0.95rem;
			margin: 0 0 2rem;
		}

		.prose h2 {
			font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.6vw, 1.5rem);
			margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
		}

		.prose h2:first-of-type {
			margin-top: 0;
		}

		.prose p {
			font-size: 1rem;
			line-height: 1.7;
			margin: 0 0 1rem;
		}

		.prose ul {
			margin: 0 0 1rem;
			padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 0.5rem;
		}

		.prose li {
			font-size: 1rem;
			line-height: 1.7;
		}

		.prose__inline-link {
			background: none;
			border: 0;
			padding: 0;
			margin: 0;
			font: inherit;
			color: var(--accent);
			text-decoration: underline;
			cursor: pointer;
		}
	</style>
</Base>
